cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lifefrom-units, please cite it as below. When you use a specific conversion factor, please also cite its source (explain() returns it)."
title: "lifefrom-units: lab unit normalisation and sourced conversion"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
type: software
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://lifefrom.ai/research/open-data/lab-units"
repository-code: "https://github.com/caraulani/lifefrom-units"
authors:
  - name: LifeFrom
    website: "https://lifefrom.ai"
  - given-names: Julian
    family-names: Caraulani
    affiliation: LifeFrom
keywords:
  - laboratory medicine
  - clinical chemistry
  - units of measure
  - UCUM
  - unit conversion
  - OMOP
  - FHIR
abstract: >-
  lifefrom-units normalises the unit strings printed on clinical laboratory results and converts values
  between units. Unit-arithmetic factors are derived; analyte-specific factors (molar masses, ion
  charges, published factors, the IFCC-NGSP HbA1c master equation) carry a cited source; conversions
  that must not be done by default (for example lipoprotein(a) mg/dL to nmol/L) are refused with a reason. One JSON
  specification is shared by a Python package and a TypeScript package that pass the same 1,501 test
  vectors.
